  apps view stats --live                          # a TUI app; your edits repaint it

// --- packages/darklang/cli/docs/live.dark ---
  apps view My.Counter --live   open it, following your edits to `render` or anything it calls
                                from another terminal and it repaints

// --- packages/darklang/cli/docs/live.dark ---
The tree `render` returns paints to the terminal, to a page, or to text, so
the same view is a pane and a web page. Ctrl-S saves the model as a `val`;
`apps view My.Counter --resume <val>` starts from it.

// --- packages/darklang/cli/docs/live.dark ---
## A live host on another machine

  # there
  dark --branch feature apps enable sync    pull the branch on an interval
  dark --branch feature serve My.router
  # here
  config set live.autopush on               every save commits and pushes
  # ... edit, save; the page there changes a few seconds later



// --- packages/darklang/cli/docs/command.dark ---
          aliases = [ "views", "live-values", "autopush" ]